+## Branch status & cheap reads
+
+Until now only `mindmap_close` settled anything (the whole map), so open loops
+only grew and `mindmap_get` re-sent every node in full. Migration `0044` adds
+per-node status to `memory_map_membership`:
+
+```
+status                 text not null default 'open'   -- open | resolved | dropped
+resolution_summary     text null                      -- 1..500 chars
+resolved_by_memory_id  uuid null references memories(id) on delete set null
+resolved_by_party      text null                      -- owner | model
+resolved_at            timestamptz null
+```
+
+A CHECK keeps it consistent: `open` ⇒ all resolution columns NULL; settled ⇒
+summary, party and time present. **Status is the only source of truth for
+"settled"** — never inferred from `reference_kind`; a `resolves-under` edge
+drawn by `mindmap_link` alone does not settle a node. `memory_map_events` gets an
+`(root_memory_id, id)` index; the event id is the map's **cursor**.
+
+`mindmap_get` reads are cheap by default: `include="open"` (settled branches as
+compact `resolved` entries), `depth="summary"` (content cut at
+`SUMMARY_CHARS=200` + `…`, `truncated=true`), always a `cursor`; `since=<cursor>`
+returns only nodes touched since (nothing changed → empty). `include="all"` and
+`depth="full"` opt out. `open_loops` = open members with
+`metadata.responsible_party` ∈ {owner, model}, computed over the whole map.
+
